# Copy this file to .secret-scan-local (gitignored) and list YOUR patterns:
# one case-insensitive extended regex per line, # comments allowed.
#
# This is the deny-list for the personal-content class in
# scripts/secret-scan.sh. It catches what the shape-based matchers cannot,
# because these things have no shape to match on:
#
#   · your own name, and your bare username with no leading slash (the
#     identifier class only recognises the /Users/<name> form, so a username
#     sitting on its own in a path fragment, a log line, or a URL sails past)
#   · places you live or work, and the names of people around you
#   · vendors, account nicknames, and reference numbers
#   · private repo or project code names that must not appear in a public tree
#
# A regex finds these only once you have named them, and only you can name
# them. That makes the list itself personal data, which is why the real file is
# gitignored and never ships. CI has no such file, so the class reports as
# SKIPPED there rather than as clean; local pre-commit is where it earns its
# keep, on the machine that knows its own names.
#
# Everything below is invented. Delete it and write your own.
#
# jcitizen
# jane citizen
# exampletown
# acme renovations
# holiday fund saver
# \b1234567\b
